import{_ as a,o as i,c as t,ao as n}from"./chunks/framework.Dpykwnwc.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"API design","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"api/api.md","filePath":"api/api.md","lastUpdated":null}'),s={name:"api/api.md"};function o(r,e,l,c,p,d){return i(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="API-design" tabindex="-1">API design <a class="header-anchor" href="#API-design" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;API design {#API-design}&quot;">​</a></h1><p>This part of the documentation is intended for users that want to change the internals of BMO. You can develop the package locally by typing <code>] dev BeamletOptics</code> in the REPL. An overview of all relevant topics is provided below. The following sections assume that you are in principle familiar with the concept of rays and beams, as well as optical elements – e.g. mirrors – in the context of this package. If not, it is recommended that you read the <a href="/BeamletOptics.jl/stable/basics/rays#Rays">Rays</a>, <a href="/BeamletOptics.jl/stable/basics/beams/overview#Beams">Beams</a> and <a href="/BeamletOptics.jl/stable/basics/components/components#Optical-components">Optical components</a> sections first.</p><div class="warning custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">Warning</p><p>The developer section is constantly changing as we iterate on the pre-1.0 BMO releases. If you find any outdated information, please open an issue!</p></div><ul><li><a href="./conventions#conventions">Conventions</a><ul><li><a href="./conventions#Global-optical-axis">Global optical axis</a></li><li><a href="./conventions#Right-handedness">Right handedness</a></li><li><a href="./conventions#Counter-clockwise-rotation">Counter clockwise rotation</a></li><li><a href="./conventions#Normal-vector-direction">Normal vector direction</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="./core#Core-design">Core design</a><ul><li><a href="./core#Intersect-Interact-Repeat-Loop">Intersect Interact Repeat Loop</a></li><li><a href="./core#intersections">Intersections</a></li><li><a href="./core#interactions">Interactions</a></li><li><a href="./core#hints">Hints</a></li><li><a href="./core#Tracing-logic">Tracing logic</a></li><li><a href="./core#CPU-and-GPU-support">CPU and GPU support</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="./geometry#Geometry-representation">Geometry representation</a><ul><li><a href="./geometry#Separation-of-geometry-and-optical-interactions">Separation of geometry and optical interactions</a></li><li><a href="./geometry#Single-and-multi-shaped-objects">Single and multi shaped objects</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="./meshes#meshes">Meshes</a><ul><li><a href="./meshes#Moeller-Trumbore-algorithm">Moeller Trumbore algorithm</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="./sdfs#Signed-Distance-Functions-(SDFs)">Signed Distance Functions (SDFs)</a><ul><li><a href="./sdfs#Ray-marching-algorithm">Ray marching algorithm</a></li><li><a href="./sdfs#Composite-SDFs">Composite SDFs</a></li><li><a href="./sdfs#Conic-and-aspheric-surfaces">Conic and aspheric surfaces</a></li><li><a href="./sdfs#Convex-polygon-prisms">Convex polygon prisms</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="./kinematics_api#Kinematic-system">Kinematic system</a><ul><li><a href="./kinematics_api#Kinematic-traits">Kinematic traits</a></li><li><a href="./kinematics_api#Static-and-movable-entities">Static and movable entities</a></li><li><a href="./kinematics_api#Oriented-and-directed-frames">Oriented and directed frames</a></li><li><a href="./kinematics_api#Type-specific-implementation-requirements">Type specific implementation requirements</a></li><li><a href="./kinematics_api#Shared-parts">Shared parts</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="./beams#Beams-and-sources">Beams and sources</a><ul><li><a href="./beams#Beam-interface">Beam interface</a></li><li><a href="./beams#Tracing-a-beamlet">Tracing a beamlet</a></li><li><a href="./beams#Interface-contracts">Interface contracts</a></li><li><a href="./beams#Source-sampling">Source sampling</a></li><li><a href="./beams#Solving-a-beam-group-internally">Solving a beam group internally</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="./components#Implementing-components">Implementing components</a><ul><li><a href="./components#Hooks-called-during-a-solve">Hooks called during a solve</a></li><li><a href="./components#Interaction-of-the-component-families">Interaction of the component families</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="./detectors#Detector-internals">Detector internals</a><ul><li><a href="./detectors#Hit-recording">Hit recording</a></li><li><a href="./detectors#Readout-pipeline">Readout pipeline</a></li><li><a href="./detectors#OpticsBase-extension-internals">OpticsBase extension internals</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="./rendering#Rendering-internals">Rendering internals</a><ul><li><a href="./rendering#Live-rendering-dispatch">Live rendering dispatch</a></li><li><a href="./rendering#Updating-a-handle">Updating a handle</a></li><li><a href="./rendering#Render-handle-protocol">Render handle protocol</a></li></ul></li></ul><h2 id="Public-API-for-dependent-packages" tabindex="-1">Public API for dependent packages <a class="header-anchor" href="#Public-API-for-dependent-packages" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Public API for dependent packages {#Public-API-for-dependent-packages}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Besides the exported names, a few names are declared <code>public</code> in <code>src/Exports.jl</code> without being exported, e.g. the progress interface <code>BeamletOptics.ProgressSink</code>, the sampling of the sources <code>BeamletOptics.AbstractSourceSampling</code> (see <a href="/BeamletOptics.jl/stable/api/beams#Source-sampling">Source sampling</a>) and the samplings of a detector <code>BeamletOptics.AbstractDetectorSampling</code> with <code>BeamletOptics.sample_points</code> and its result <code>BeamletOptics.DetectorSamples</code> (see <a href="/BeamletOptics.jl/stable/api/detectors#Readout-pipeline">Readout pipeline</a>), the optional <code>BeamletOptics.bounding_sphere_of</code> of a shape (see <a href="/BeamletOptics.jl/stable/api/core#Bounding-sphere-pretest">Bounding sphere pretest</a>), <code>BeamletOptics.AbstractObjectGroup</code> with <code>BeamletOptics.check_kinematic_members</code> for own assembly types of separate parts (see <a href="/BeamletOptics.jl/stable/basics/kinematics/objects#Assemblies:-group-or-multi-shape-object">Assemblies: group or multi-shape object</a>), or <code>BeamletOptics.relaunch!</code> and the beamlet hit records (<code>BeamletOptics.AstigmaticGaussianBeamletHit(agb, id)</code>, <code>electric_field(hit, p)</code>) for components that re-emit light, e.g. solvers coupled through a field (see <a href="/BeamletOptics.jl/stable/api/core#Re-emitting-components">Re-emitting components</a>). Packages built on BMO, such as <a href="https://github.com/StackEnjoyer/BeamletOpticsGUI.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">BeamletOpticsGUI</a>, may rely on them like on the exported API; other unexported names are internal and may change in any release. Whether a name is public can be checked with <code>Base.ispublic(BeamletOptics, name)</code>. Their docstrings are listed in the <a href="/BeamletOptics.jl/stable/reference#Reference">Reference</a>, the render handle protocol is described in <a href="/BeamletOptics.jl/stable/api/rendering#Render-handle-protocol">Render handle protocol</a>. A new <code>AbstractObject</code> subtype can add a method of <a href="/BeamletOptics.jl/stable/basics/components/components#BeamletOptics.properties-basics-components-components"><code>BeamletOptics.properties</code></a> to list its own parameters (<code>properties</code> and <code>default_properties</code> are public, not exported: write <code>BeamletOptics.properties</code>), see <a href="/BeamletOptics.jl/stable/basics/components/components#Inspecting-components">Inspecting components</a>.</p>',6)])])}const f=a(s,[["render",o]]);export{h as __pageData,f as default};
